.TH tapectl 1  "tapectl 1.8.1" 
.SH NAME
tapectl \- Multi\-tenant archival storage management for LTO tape and exportable encrypted directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Multi\-tenant archival storage management for LTO tape and exportable encrypted directories
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
No live progress on stderr. Long operations (stage create, volume write/resume/verify/read\-slices, restore) still write their session log under <home>/logs/
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, stage reports. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home.
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, stage\-reports, logs.

The home is the first of: \-\-home; TAPECTL_HOME; the directory of \-\-config; this account\*(Aqs ~/.tapectl, when it exists; the home named by the home pointer /etc/tapectl/home (TAPECTL_HOME_POINTER names another file), when the account has no ~/.tapectl of its own; else ~/.tapectl, where `tapectl init` makes a new one. The config file is <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config names another. `tapectl status` and `tapectl config check` name the home in use and the rule that chose it.

As root the home pointer is never read, and on a host that has one tapectl refuses unless \-\-home or TAPECTL_HOME names the home: the service user\*(Aqs commands run through `tapectl\-op`.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tapectl\-init(1)
Initialize tapectl (DB, config, operator tenant, keys, and the permanent escrow recipient — ADR\-0005; use \-\-no\-escrow to skip it, or \-\-escrow\-public\-key to adopt an existing one instead of minting a new identity)
.TP
tapectl\-tenant(1)
Manage tenants
.TP
tapectl\-key(1)
Manage encryption keys
.TP
tapectl\-unit(1)
Manage archival units
.TP
tapectl\-collection(1)
Manage media collections (folder=unit factory + batch tape driver)
.TP
tapectl\-snapshot(1)
Manage snapshots
.TP
tapectl\-stage(1)
Stage snapshots for writing
.TP
tapectl\-volume(1)
Manage volumes and tape operations
.TP
tapectl\-cartridge(1)
Manage physical cartridges
.TP
tapectl\-archive\-set(1)
Manage archive set policies
.TP
tapectl\-audit(1)
Policy compliance audit
.TP
tapectl\-catalog(1)
Browse and search file catalog
.TP
tapectl\-location(1)
Manage storage locations
.TP
tapectl\-report(1)
Generate reports
.TP
tapectl\-restore(1)
Restore data from volumes
.TP
tapectl\-quick\-archive(1)
Quick archive: create + stage + write in one flow
.TP
tapectl\-drive(1)
The tape drive: declare one (`drive add`), what is in it now (`drive status`), eject it (`drive eject`), its health on a schedule (`drive poll`), its cleanings (`drive cleaned`)
.TP
tapectl\-db(1)
Database operations
.TP
tapectl\-config(1)
Configuration management
.TP
tapectl\-host(1)
This host\*(Aqs fitness to feed a tape drive (the quiet\-host check)
.TP
tapectl\-status(1)
The home screen: the home and why it was chosen, what is running, the units by state, the volumes due a verify, and the next commands
.TP
tapectl\-completions(1)
Generate shell completions
.TP
tapectl\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v1.8.1
